      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, very good point. The onAvailable and onLost are covered in the rematch but what about onCapabilitiesChanged? To that end, that\u0027s actually covered in notifyNetworkCallbacks() on l.8319 in patch 7. The reason I am confident in this is actually due to test failures when I was verifying these changes.\n\nIf you look at this new test in a follow-up CL, you\u0027ll see that we are calling this existing test method: \n defaultNetworkCallback.expectAvailableThenValidatedCallbacks(mEthernetNetworkAgent);\n\nhttps://r.android.com/c/platform/frameworks/base/+/1579208/12/tests/net/java/com/android/server/ConnectivityServiceTest.java#9882\n\nI originally only had changes in the onAvailable and onLost portions of code and this test failed because it also checked for \u0027validated\u0027 which looks to come from the onCapabilitiesChanged event. I then had to modify notifyNetworkCallbacks() on l.8319 which allowed this code to fire for onCapabilitiesChanged (as well as other events) and after that the test passed.\n\nThat said, it looks like what I have is working from what I can tell and the complexity doesn\u0027t seem to bad (IMO). Happy to discuss more but it looks like the above is covered.",
