      "writtenOn": "2021-02-10T22:57:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, good point. This is currently the only situation where an app\u0027s default network callback won\u0027t fire. \n\nConsider OEM_PAID preference:\n \n unmetered -\u003e oem_paid (restricted) -\u003e default network\n\nFor both the unmetered and default networks, the apps own TRACK_DEFAULT callbacks will trigger on their own with no intervention by this code. Therefore in those cases, AFAIK we don\u0027t need/want to send a callback as it would be an additional one.\n\nThe only situation therefore we have to account for is restricted networks which won\u0027t trigger for TRACK_DEFAULT.\n\nNow, we could have increased the complexity here to try and generalize this code, however the increased complexity outweighed (IMO) the benefit considering I don\u0027t imagine the above changing anytime soon and if it does, it would be better to adjust then once we have the concrete requirements available therefore I opted to reduce the complexity and handle the one scenario where TRACK_DEFAULT requests won\u0027t fire on their own.",
